# ── Model weights via Git LFS ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# These are regenerated on every training run. Left in regular git they add a
# full copy of each artifact to history per run — 4.5 MB today, but linear in
# the number of retrains, and every clone pays for all of it forever.
#
# LFS stores a pointer in git and the blob out of band, so history stays small
# and only the checked-out revision is fetched.
#
# NOTE: blobs committed BEFORE this file existed remain in normal git object
# storage. That is deliberate — converting them requires rewriting history, and
# 4.5 MB is not worth a rewrite. Everything committed from here on uses LFS.
machine_learning/artifacts/*.joblib   filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
machine_learning/artifacts/*.pt       filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
machine_learning/artifacts/*.npy      filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
machine_learning/artifacts/*.pkl      filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
machine_learning/artifacts/*.onnx     filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text

# ── Line endings ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
* text=auto eol=lf
*.sh   text eol=lf
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.pdf  binary
